Executive Summary  
The notes for WW20'26 focus on negotiations and compliance related to GPS and WiFi/GPS bundles. The team is seeking data to assess bundle value, aiming for a 10% discount, and considering alternative options if a better deal cannot be secured before year-end. There is an emphasis on getting AOS to properly value the WiFi/GPS bundles.

---

### Key Points
- 100% compliance achieved on GPS bundles (credit given to a team member).
- Data requested on WiFi/GPS bundles vs. GPS-only to assess bundle value.
- Need for AOS to recognize the value of WiFi/GPS bundles.
- Negotiation for a 10% discount on bundle price.
- Exploring other options if a better deal is not secured.
- Target to secure improved deal before end of year.

### Decisions
- None

### Action Items
- Request data on WiFi/GPS bundles vs. GPS-only (owner not specified).
- Get AOS to value WiFi/GPS bundles (owner not specified).
- Negotiate for a 10% discount on bundle price (owner not specified).

### Risks/Blockers
- Potential inability to secure a better deal before year-end.
- AOS may not properly value WiFi/GPS bundles.

### Open Questions
- Who owns each action item?
- What are the alternative options if a better deal is not secured?
- What specific data is needed for bundle valuation?

